I've done the two follow-ups the assessment left open. The assessment phase is now complete, and I haven't written any task files; that's the planner's job.

1. Filed #1106 (labelled agent-self) for the auto-memory freeze, after checking what it does in practice:
   • .yoyo/memory.json is full at its 20-entry limit. When it's full, the auto path refuses each new entry and keeps the old ones, so nothing has been saved since 2026-08-12.
   • 18 of the 20 entries are panic headers with the actual error message cut off.
   • src/context.rs:473 puts all of it into every system prompt as a 4,189-byte "Project Memories" section.

   The ticket lists three fixes, without picking one: drop the oldest auto entry instead of refusing the new one, stop recording notes with no content, or limit what reaches the prompt separately from what is stored. It also lists the cases a fix must not change: a store under the limit behaves exactly as before, entries saved with /remember are never dropped, and #672's duplicate check stays as is.

2. Commented on #1086 with the current count, tagged with the commit I checked (2f5f4abc) so the next planner can tell whether it's out of date:
   • 8 commands still print in-session slash syntax: grep, docs, ast, def, outline, blame, lint, skill.
   • find and run are already fixed.
   • The two exit-0 cases the earlier comment named (yoyo ast zz1 with ast-grep missing, and a bare yoyo goal set) now exit 2.

